<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Eldredgeops rana_17file Turing wavelength at 342 nm (Tioughniogan, 384 Ma) (Eldredgeops rana_17file)",
        "Eldredgeops rana_17file Turing wavelength at 342 nm (Tioughniogan, 384 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eldredgeops rana_17file morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eldredgeops rana_17file specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eldredgeops rana_17file" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 342 nm was measured on a Tioughniogan lens.",
        "does_not_claim: That a second independent assessor has scored this script.",
        "does_not_claim: That the self-similar predecessor wavelength 323 nm is the law used here.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Predecessor cell side scaled by 17/18 at fixed lambda_c = 342 nm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Quadratic optical readout I = c0 + c1 u_hat + c2 v_hat + c3 u_hat^2 + c4 v_hat^2 fit to the plate's radial luminance.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters rho_a=0.082, rho_b=0.918, D_u=0.060, D_v=1.200, periodic cell 1.15 lambda_c, seed 3216.",
        "reported_in_source: Eldredge 1972 documents a step from 18 to 17 dorsoventral lens files between the Cazenovian and Tioughniogan horizons.",
        "reported_in_source: Lindgren et al. 2019 show a screening pigment associated with fossil arthropod eyes, which is the anatomical context for a pigment-ring wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber when the two morphogens diffuse at different rates.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery plate is a radial ocellus field with a labeled 100 micrometre bar (measured 111 px, 0.901 µm/px). Comparison is dimensionless radial shape plus computer-vision texture, not a claim that the plate's field of view is 342 nm." ;
